{"name":"Bruised Plum","hex":"#3b1921","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bruised","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of bruise"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Synonym of debruised."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bruised"},{"term":"plum","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fruit and its tree.\n An edible, fleshy stone fruit of species Prunus domestica (European plum) and Prunus americana American plum, often of a dark red or purple colour. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\nA stone-fruit tree which bears this fruit, Prunus domestica. \nThe edible, fleshy stone fruit of several species resembling the plum, or the tree from which they grow. \nPrunus sect. Prunus\nPrunus cerasifera (cherry plum or myrobalan).\nPrunus salicina (Chinese plum or Japanese plum).\nPrunus spinosa (sloe).\nPrunus ursina (bear's plum).\nPrunus sect. Prunocerasus (North American plums)\nPrunus americana (American plum).\nPrunus angustifolia (Chickasaw plum or sand plum).\nPrunus hortulana (hortulan plum).\nPrunus nigra (Canadian plum or black plum).\nPrunus rivularis (creek plum or hog plum).\nPrunus subcordata (Klamath plum or Oregon plum).\nPrunus sect. Armeniaca (better known as apricots)\nPrunus mume, an Asian fruit more closely related to the apricot than the plum, usually consumed pickled, dried, or as a juice or wine; ume.\n A dried grape or raisin, as used in a pudding or cake.","An edible, fleshy stone fruit of species Prunus domestica (European plum) and Prunus americana American plum, often of a dark red or purple colour. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a dark bluish-red colour.","Choice; especially lavish or preferred."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bruise","blocks":[{"text":"A bruise, also known as a contusion, is a type of hematoma of tissue, the most common cause being capillaries damaged by trauma, causing localized bleeding that extravasates into the surrounding interstitial tissues. Most bruises occur close enough to the epidermis such that the bleeding causes a visible discoloration. The bruise then remains visible until the blood is either absorbed by tissues or cleared by immune system action. Bruises which do not blanch under pressure can involve capillaries at the level of skin, subcutaneous tissue, muscle, or bone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Pferdekuss.jpg/330px-Pferdekuss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruise","wikidata":"Q574491"},{"title":"Plum","blocks":[{"text":"A plum is a fruit of some species in Prunus subg. Prunus. Dried plums are usually called prunes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg/330px-Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum","wikidata":"Q12372598"},{"title":"Plum (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Plum is a purple color with a brownish-gray tinge, like that shown on the right, or a reddish purple, which is a close representation of the average color of the plum fruit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Plum_on_tree02.jpg/330px-Plum_on_tree02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum_(color)","wikidata":"Q3108722"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg/500px-Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg/500px-Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A woman's bruising after a severe fall","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Severebruise.jpg/500px-Severebruise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Severebruise.jpg/1280px-Severebruise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Severebruise.jpg/500px-Severebruise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bruise caused by colliding with a handrail, typical of extreme sports such as skateboarding and rollerblading.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeverebruise.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sprained_foot.jpg/500px-Sprained_foot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sprained_foot.jpg/1280px-Sprained_foot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sprained_foot.jpg/500px-Sprained_foot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bruise caused by a sprained ankle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASprained_foot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ca/Blaues_und_rotes_Auge_nach_Fu%C3%9Ftritt_ins_Gesicht_%28Ausschnitt%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ca/Blaues_und_rotes_Auge_nach_Fu%C3%9Ftritt_ins_Gesicht_%28Ausschnitt%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Black eye and subconjunctival hemorrhage after a punch to th